## 3. The 3-Signal Scoring Model

Every candidate attraction is assigned a total score between **0 and 16 points**:

$$\text{Total Score} = \text{static\_weight} + \text{category\_behaviour\_weight} + \text{region\_behaviour\_weight}$$

| Signal | Source | Max Points | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Signal 1: `static_weight`** | Registration User Preferences | **+6 pts** | Match against `travelStyle` (+3), `environment` (+2), and `activities` (+1 each, max 3). |
| **Signal 2: `category_behaviour_weight`** | Global 60-day Tap Logs | **+5 pts** | Tap count on matching category across all locations ($1 \text{ tap} = +1\text{ pt}$, capped at 5). |
| **Signal 3: `region_behaviour_weight`** | Context-Scoped Region Logs | **+5 pts** | Tap count on matching region type **ONLY IF** candidate region matches current context ($1 \text{ tap} = +1\text{ pt}$, capped at 5). |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Context Gate Rule**:
> $$\text{region\_behaviour\_weight} = \begin{cases} \min(\text{taps in candidate region}, 5), & \text{if } \text{itemRegionType} == \text{currentContextRegion} \\ 0, & \text{otherwise} \end{cases}$$

